# Issue #1021 — `spec/grammar.md:34`: "Within a single expression, list literal, dict literal, or
# parenthesized group, newlines are insignificant." The branch decision that picks
# `parenthesized-expression` (grammar.md:213) over `parenthesized-call` (:215) therefore looks PAST
# any newlines between the head and the operator, so a group written across lines reads exactly as
# its one-line form.
#
# This fixture exists because the newline-skipping is otherwise proven only inside the TypeScript
# unit suite: deleting the skip leaves all 931 stack-neutral fixtures passing. The conformance
# corpus is the proof meant to outlive this implementation, so the guarantee belongs in it.
define six
  return 6
end
print (pi
== pi)
print (six
+ 1)
print (six
* 2)
